      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with an ankle sprain without signs of a fracture do well once it's treated properly. I think an ankle X-ray makes sense here, for ankle injury. You'll be taking paracetamol, 1 gram, every six hours if needed, for five days. It's for ankle pain. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well.",
